"P601379215" "Pik'Tarn's story"
// DetailString :
"P314177369" "When you defeated the Rikti warrior Pik'Tarn, he gasped: <br><br>'Circle:Draws Closed. His Past: Our Future.' <br><br>It could be that this has something to do with Timothy's lost memories."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MysticTome 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3613393383" "Mystic tome"
// DetailString :
"P236571528" "This tome, titled 'On the Human Mind: Unlocking its Secrets,' seems promising. It may well help you restore Timothy's memory."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Embryos 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1823878604" "Test tube embryos"
// DetailString :
"P3753414293" "You found hundreds of embryos inside a refrigerator in a secret Rikti lab. All are marked with Timothy Raymond's name, and with the names of various Rikti females. It seems clear that the Rikti have used Timothy's stolen DNA to create a new generation of aliens! <br><br>The strangest thing is, the embryos appear entirely human. They have no resemblance to the Rikti's grey, bony bodies."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2854066389" "Strange Memories"
// DetailString :
"P150108428" "It began with a sudden resurgence of Timothy Raymond's memory: he recalled a secret Rikti base in Primeva. You ventured there, and defeated the Rikti inside, but were left with questions. The Rikti leader seemed to remember Timothy, but you had no idea what this might mean. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1314896363" "It began with a sudden resurgence of Timothy Raymond's memory: he recalled a secret Rikti base in Primeva. You ventured there, and defeated the Rikti inside, but were left with questions. The Rikti leader seemed to remember Timothy, but you had no idea what this might mean. <br><br>Timothy's frustration with his lost memory reached a peak then. He decided he was tired of waiting for Arachnos to help him recover his memory. Instead, he sent you to a Circle of Thorns base, where you stole a tome that would help him regain his memories. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL5_NA_Timothy_Raymond_MiniArc 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2272798345" "Rikti embryo"
// tDetailString :
"P1204885679" "You've kept this Rikti embryo fertilized with human DNA as a reminder of an unusual adventure you like to think of as: <br><br>Strange Memories <br><br>It began with a sudden resurgence of Timothy Raymond's memory: he recalled a secret Rikti base in Primeva. You ventured there, and defeated the Rikti inside, but were left with questions. The Rikti leader seemed to remember Timothy, but you had no idea what this might mean. <br><br>Timothy's frustration with his lost memory reached a peak then. He decided he was tired of waiting for Arachnos to help him recover his memory. Instead, he sent you to a Circle of Thorns base, where you stole a tome that would help him regain his memories. <br><br>The spells contained within the tome worked, and Timothy remembered something more: his DNA had been stolen by the Rikti. He sent you to investigate, and what you uncovered was horrible and fascinating at the same time. The Rikti had used Timothy's DNA to fertilize a number of Rikti embryos. You could only assume his latent psionic gifts were somehow of use to them. <br><br>You smuggled the embryos away, and gave most of them to Timothy, who immediately resolved to incinerate them. Before he sent you away, he parted with one final secret, the last thing he had remembered. Rikti were people. Somehow, humans and Rikti shared a common genetic heritage. You're not sure of the full implications of this secret, but you know it's a valuable one."

